## CURRENT STATE
- D1–D9 CLOSED. D10 Admin Area is complete and merged into `main` from `d10-admin-area-complete`, based on `b1315e509e6343bdcef326ee59fe8cc04d9d0583`.
- The Admin Area was reused, not rebuilt: `/admin`, `ModerationPanelClient`, `usePhase9Moderation`, the Supabase moderation service, the report queue, report events and internal notes, the moderation actions, the listing transitions, the dispute queue and the append-only audit log are the Phase 9 ones. No `moderation_v2`, no second report table, no second audit system, no parallel admin queue.
- `/admin` decides on the server. `frontend-next/src/app/admin/page.tsx` awaits `connection()`, resolves the session through the existing server auth helper, reads `user_roles` and calls `notFound()` unless the caller really holds `admin`; an absent session redirects to `/accedi`. No `service_role` key is used in the page or anywhere in the browser.
- The demo switcher grants nothing. `ModerationPanelClient` and the shell navigation both read `authRuolo` (the real role from `user_roles`) instead of the demo `ruolo`, so selecting "Admin" in the demo UI opens no admin surface.
- D9 review reports reach moderators through the existing reports system: `recensione` is a `report_target_tipo` value and `reports.target_review_id` references `public.order_reviews`, both from Phase 9a. No D9-specific queue was added.
- Migration `20260828120000_d10_admin_dispute_gate.sql` adds `public.moderazione_contestazione_risolvi(uuid, text, text)`: `SECURITY DEFINER`, `SET search_path = ''`, mandatory `auth.uid()`, mandatory real admin role, server-validated order, mandatory bounded note, `jsonb` return.
- `EXECUTE` on that door is revoked from `PUBLIC`, `anon` **and** `service_role`, and granted to `authenticated` alone. `service_role` is named in the revoke because the Supabase project carries an `alter default privileges ... grant all on functions to ... service_role`: omitting it from the grant list does not withhold it. Verified on the local instance — without that revoke the resulting ACL is `postgres=X/postgres service_role=X/postgres authenticated=X/postgres`. The door requires `auth.uid()`, which a service key does not carry, so the permission was unusable as well as unintended.
- The browser-admin door accepts only `risolta` and `respinta`. `p_esito` is `text` against a closed list, so `rimborsata` is not a legal input rather than a legal value stopped by a check. The frozen `public.ordine_contestazione_risolvi` was not modified and remains available to `service_role`; the new door calls it internally and writes nothing to `orders`, `payouts`, `payments` or `disputes` itself.
- The Controversie tab is operational for `aperta` and `in_valutazione` practices: "Risolvi" and "Respingi", a required motivation, per-row in-flight state that blocks double submission, mediated errors and a queue reload after success. Terminal practices expose no action. There is no "Rimborsa" button; refund and provider actions remain OFF.
- The disposable grid `supabase/tests/d10_admin_area.sql` passes 40/40 across LETTURE, D9, AZIONI, PORTA, ESITI, DENARO, IDEMPOTENZA and ESPOSIZIONE, on a local Docker Supabase database holding every preceding migration, with all 17 residue counters at zero and both append-only guards re-enabled. Case 34 asserts the absence of the `service_role` privilege, not only the presence of the `authenticated` one.
- The full `frontend-next` suite passes 1256/1256 across 77 files, and typecheck is clean. `MIN_TESTS` was raised from `1224` to `1256` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `prelaunch-contract.test.ts` in the same change, as raising one alone fails CI.
- One assertion in `navigazione-mobile.test.ts` pinned the whole `useVinea()` destructuring line while its subject is that `autenticato` has a single source. It now matches that subject — `ruolo` present in the destructuring, `autenticato` assigned exactly once — so reading another field from the same hook no longer fails it.
- No production read, write, fixture or deployment. Phase 13 cutover has not started.

